The '''Hydian Way''' was a [[super-hyperroute]] established by [[Freia Kallea]] in [[3705 BBY]]. Beginning at [[Bonadan]] in the [[Corporate Sector]], it ran inward to the [[Core Worlds]] and then back out to end at the [[Imynusoph system]] in the southern [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]].

==History==
{{Quote|We shall reinforce our fleet along the Hydian Way. This should prevent Grievous from&mdash;|Jedi Master Plo Koon|<ref name="R2 Come Home">{{TCW|R2 Come Home}}</ref>}}
In [[3705 BBY]], the Hydian Way was established by [[Freia Kallea]].<ref name="BMF 29" /> In time, it became the biggest trade route in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Bounty Hunters 6">[[Bounty Hunters 6|''Bounty Hunters'' 6]]</ref>

Sometime after the [[Defeat of the Sith|fall]] of the [[Sith]]<ref name="Trkn" /> in [[1032 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the [[Core Worlds|Core World]] of [[Corulag]] influenced the route so that it would include the space around the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Eriadu]] on its path in order to force the planet to produce shipments of [[lommite]] ore more regularly. Eriadu was later able to transform itself into a major trade world, partly due to the fact that it lay at the confluence of the Hydian Way and the [[Rimma Trade Route]]. When [[Wilhuff Tarkin]], a young student of the [[Sullust Sector Spacefarers Academy]], first met [[Senator]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]], he requested aid in enforcing law in the [[Greater Seswenna]] region around Eriadu as he believed doing so could ease tensions along the entire Hydian Way.<ref name="Trkn" />

During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Jedi Master]] [[Plo Koon]] made plans to bolster the [[Galactic Republic]] [[fleet]] along the Hydian Way in an effort to halt the efforts of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[General]] [[Grievous]].<ref name="R2 Come Home" />

Much later in Tarkin's life, his personal [[corvette]], the ''[[Carrion Spike]]'', was [[Mission to Murkhana|stolen]] by a [[Berch Teller's rebel cell|rebel cell]] who used it to [[Berch Teller campaign|attack]] several [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] targets. While the [[Starship|ship]] was still at large, the Empire deployed additional forces along both the Hydian Way and the Rimma Trade Route in order to try and fend off further attacks.<ref name="Trkn" />

At one point, [[Han Solo]] and [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian]] met up with the [[Tonnika sisters]] in a casino ship in the Hydian Way.<ref name="Princess and the Scoundrel">''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]''</ref>

The [[planet]] [[Dathomir]] was near the Hydian Way and the [[Salin Corridor]].<ref name="Dawn">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref>

